  "chapter": 375,
  "signer": "ANDREW M. CUOMO",
  "text": "\n \n                APPROVAL MEMORANDUM - No. 68 Chapter 375\n \n        MEMORANDUM filed with Senate Bill Number 8828, entitled:\n \n    \"AN ACT to amend the labor law, in relation to establishing a regis-\n        try  of  workplace  fatalities  in  the construction industry to\n        record information pertaining to all incidents  under  which  an\n        employee  performing  construction  work  suffers a work-related\n        fatal injury\"\n \n    APPROVED\n \n  The bill requires the Department of Labor  to  create  a  registry  of\nworkplace  fatalities  in  the construction industry. The information in\nthe registry would include information reported to DOL by county  coron-\ners,  medical examiners, and employers. I support the goals of this bill\nto make information available about workers who are killed while working\nin the construction industry. I  have  secured  an  agreement  with  the\nLegislature  to  make  certain  technical changes to the bill, including\nextending the effective date. On the  basis  of  this  agreement,  I  am\npleased to sign this bill.\n \n  The bill is approved.                       (signed) ANDREW M. CUOMO\n \n                                ______\n",
  "year": 2020
 },
